>Subject:	 CAMPUS  INTERVIEWS
>
>Hello friends,
>      I'm attaching here with some questions that had been asked
>during campus interviews to our batch and to seniour batch. Hope it
>will be useful to you.
>Wishing you  the best
>[Madhusudhana.C.S]
>.............................................................
>TISL interview was conducted in a rather shady manner at the CSIC.
>The written test was an aptitude test and i was told later that the
>cutoff
>for H/W was kept higher than that for S/W. Only CEDT guys were
>interviewed
>for H/w probably because we had campaigned for the jobs at the PPT.
>
>The Interview at CSIC was by a single guy who asked me about my
>project
>and then about PC architecture. Knowledge from douglas hall sufficed
>to
>answer all his questions.
>
>Then we were asked to meet some people at TISL office where we were
>interviewed by three different people. one guy ( the BOSS Aditya
>srinivasan ) just asked some general questions on our projects.
>The other two ( Ajay Tambe & Yogesh Dayal )were more detailed and
>asked
>about IC used, PC fundas , elementary digital design and some analog
>design ( designing astables etc..).
>
>TISL recruits H/W mtechs for their IPTS group.this group does h/w
>design
>for IBM AUSTIN, IBM Europe and IBM Japan. The group is at present
>30-40
>people strong and are a bit different from the general S/w guys. some
>CEDT
>seniors at that place SAJJID ( sajid@genius.tisl.soft.net) and a guy
>called kiran( RAvi?). They have said that the work is OK and chances
>of
>going abroad are also good.
>
>************************************************************
>                 TI
>Make an OR gate using a two input mux.
>Make a JK F/F from a four input mux and a D F/F.
>How will u synchronize an asynchronous signal?
>        -using a D F/F ? ...How will u take care of setup time  & hold
>time
>How will u delay a serial synchronous data by 64 bits?
>Implement the following logic:
>      Read operation should have one wait state
>      & write operation should have two
>Some more digital logic
>
>Types of feedback.
>OP-AMP configeration in these types.
>
>Cmos inverter: ckt diag; allowable voltages at the input; threshold
>voltage;
>    graph of input Vs output voltage .....currents....
>
>And some project
>                 infotech
>
>Setup time, hold time, meta-stable state
>What is noise margin?
>How will u implement single steping using the ready pin?
>Draw the timing cycles (read & Write) of 8086.
>And some project
>i don't remember any more.
>Ask others also to send some questions, u will get a lot more.
>***********************************************************
>Non-technical:
>* Tell me something about ur self ( May be u can prepare something
>for this before hand)
>* What is it do u consider ur biggest plus point ? ( Substantiate
>with an example incident rather than giving a blanket reply)
>* biggest minus point ? ( Up to u to tell them ur real minus point or
>a cooked up "minus point")
>* After 5 years from now what would u want to be ? ( Project leader
>may be a suitable answer , but make sure everyone doesn't say the
>same thing)
>* What is ur rank in the class? (Tell them the exact number if u are
>within top 5 . Else may be u can simply telll them u are within top x
>* Why does CEDT offer M.Tech while other depts offer M.E. ? i.e. what
>differentiates an M.Tech Degree from M.E.? ( courtesy Cadence)
>
>Technical :
>* Explain DMA
>* U have a 386 mother board which doesn't work. What will be ur
>sequence of operation for debugging the board.
>* The famous D-flip flop question.
>
>Project - related questions:
>
>* In ur project will any catastrophic situation occur at power-on due
>to ur digital circuitry taking random logical outputs?
>* What are the specifications of ur product?
>
>General suggestions:
>* Be there well ahead of ur allotted time . Chances are they may call
>u in slightly ahead too.
>* Make sure ur replies are convincing not only to u but also to the
>others. Unconvincing replies usually invite more embarrassing
>questions.
>* Take ur grade sheets along (if u have got them)
>* Don't invite the placement centre's wrath by by-passing
>the centre and contacting companies outside the campus. It is also
>unethical.
>* Select ur dream jobs well ahead of the last date for submission of
>forms to the placement centre. This is to avoid a hasty decision at
>the last minute on such an important matter.
>**************************************************************
>I. technical :
>-------------
>1. what is ur project ?
>2. which part r u handling ?
>3. what r methods to control  I.M. speed?
>4. why PWM ?
>5. why V/F ?
>6. what r critical issues involved?
>7. build 3-bit adder using 2 2-bit adders.
>8. xor gate using min. no. of NAND gates ( 4 reqd.)
>9. one example on K-map
>10. how'll u do POS in K-map?
>11. what is diff. betn DSP and other architectures?
>12. in a shift reg. 4 bit if clock to all is delayed by delays
>T1,T2,T3 and T4 , what is relation betnthem for reliable operaion?
>assume F/F delat Td all equal.
>13. how'll u build XNOR using NOR gates?
>
>II. Non-technical:
>-----------------
>1. tell us @ ur academic
>2. whta r ur + and - points? exemplify.
>3. what is motivation behind doing M.tech?
>4. why do want to join cg corel?
>5. what r qualities a designer should possess?
>6. what is more imp. for u : carrer or job atm?
>7. how many sisters / brothers u have..?
>8. why u didn't apply to infosys?
>9. what is r&d in ur opinion?
>10. do regret for your career which does not focus at a point ?
>***************************************************************
>Regarding interview questions:
>Wipro:
>     State Diagram implemention of digital logic ( eg. binary counter).
>     Cache Coherence
>     PC AT bus
>     Other high speed buses (
>     Meta stable state in FFs ( refer Art of Electronics)
>     ( nothing about the project! )
>
>TI:
>     Project :
>         my contribution to the project
>         codecs, internal block diagram of codec
>         aliasing in frequency domain
>     Design an SR FF using 2:4 Encoder
>
>TISL:
>     (Satish has sent a detailed mail, so no repititions from me)
>
>Enjoy CEDT, explore the WEB, dont feel that if you netscape your
>grades will go down.
>
>All the Best!
>******************************************************************
>dear juniors
>       The list of questions
>       1> About your project you should know every thing.
>       2> Metastable state in flip flops
>       3> pal structure 16l8,number of or term ,and term
>       4> microprocessor read and write timing diagram
>       5> how you will jmp to some location in memory where you don,t
>         have jmp and call instruction.
>       6> how nmi,interrupts are handled in processor you know
>       7>interface of floppy disk controller,interrupt controls and
>         how they work
>       8>async.data to sync data
>       9>state diagram use in designing counters
>       10>constant current source
>      this are some of the topics on which questions where ask to me
>and my friends.
>******************************************************************
>     WIPRO
>     Started with introduction and about the background [family and
>     educational].
>     Questions:
>     1] For given logic ckt with some delay,setup and hold time how
>     will you calculate the max. operating freq.?
>     2] What happens if you violets the setup and hold time
>     requirements?
>     3] How to synchronize the async. signal?
>     4]What is the main drawback of sync. ckt and how to avoid it?
>     5]Draw a ckt diagram to interface 8259 with a processor.
>     6]How interrupt mach. works for 8085 and 8086?
>     7]What is DMA and how it is advantageous over the data transfer
>     with processor involved?
>     8]What are the protocols involved in DMA transfer?
>
>Some Question related to project.
>     9]How to protect control ckt. for high freq. pickup?
>    10]What are the PCB requirements for High freq. digital ckt.
>
>
>    Thats all from WIPRO .
>    Tomorrow the questions from TI.
>    With Best Wishes
>
>*****************************************************************
>Subject:        interview
>Copies to:      EBENEZER
>
>Friends,
>I appeared for one company on campus and got selected. The company is
>Wipro Infotech Global R & D and it was my dream job....
>The company has put CGPA cutoff as 6.5 as first filter and allowed 10
>people to appear for interview. I was interviewed by 2 hardware
>experts.
>It started with general questions like my background and general
>information about previous experience. Then they turned to my M Tech
>project and asked to draw block diagram, few questions on TSI
>switching like how is done and data rates on input and output lines.
>Then few questions came on telephone lines like what is difference
>between normal telephone line and leased one? What is the max. bit
>transfer rate on these lines?
>Then one of them asked about my interests and I told communication,
>to be specific data communication and then he asked me to justify it.
>Then we talked ( for all the topics given below, it was more
>like a discussion and I simply told them how much I know in each
>of the topics ) about 7 layers of protocol. Then different types of
>networks and their protocols like ISDN, ATM, X.25, CSMA/CD, Token ring
>bit rate on each of these networks, comaprison in terms of throughput
>between token ring and csma network. We had little chat on LAN/WAN.
>Finally he asked me on which cpus I had worked.....and how much I
>knew about PC architecture and thats it............
>Then I was selected for personal interview which went for 5 minutes
>and there he asked me about my general interests, strengths and
>weaknesses. Then why wipro?????????? I was prepared for this and
>already knew some good points and achievements of the company.....
>Finally I got selected....................
>
>General Remarks:
>This interview was taken specifically for coomunication hardware and
>hence all need not consider these questions as general questions...
>Also remember following things....
>You should be abel to justify your field of interests.....
>You must know about the company before appearing for interview.
>At least one of your interests should match to the company's area of
>work.
>Be frank to say no if you really don't know.....
>Then it is not "START 0-0" but "ADAVANTAGE 'YOU'AND ONE MATCHPOINT"
>Wish you All the Best..... enjoy your life at CEDT......
>I will send you my new email ID later.
>Mangesh
>
>*********************************************************
>Hi,
>Here are some questions asked in Wipro interview.
>
>First they asked general things about my project.
>I had programmed FPGA in my project. So there were a few questions
>about how did I actually went about designing FPGA like the package
>used, device etc.
>Then some questions on Bus architecture. But I didn't knew any of
>them.
>So they turned to 8086 interrupt as to what exactly happens after
>interrupt occurs, etc.
>Finally they asked on Digital like metamorphic states in F/F.
>How to design a glitch free ckt and why exactly like that. Here some
>hypothetical ckt.
>That's all. I didn't appeared for any other interview after that.
>Last but not the least. In personal interview, they mainly check your
>probability of joining the company and they may reject you solely on
>your personal interview performance even if your technical has been
>good. So careful about that.
>
>ALL THE BEST FOR YOUR FUTURE AND CAREER PLANS.
>A. S. DATE
>Subject:       Interview questions
>Dear Juniors
>
>     Here are my interview questions, i.e. the questions people had
>asked me during the campus interviews at IISc. I feel that there will
>not be any problem with the tests, most of them are aptitude tests.
>
>     Before CG-coreEL, I had attended some ten interviews,
>after CG-coreEL none. So I may not able to recollect all the
>questions, but I'll try my best.
>
>     Most of them asks only about general things like whether you know
>this, that etc... For such questions I had just specified the topic
>as such, you just go through it and get a peripheral idea of those.
>
>     Invariably all starts with personnel questions. So be prepare for
>telling something about yourself.
>
>TISL :      test - aptitude
>             questions - Different bus architectures, [outline only]
>                         Type of memories, their differences.
>                         project related questions.
>WIPRO :     no test [ CGPA cutoff]
>             questions - Different memories
>                         On what conditions you will choose SRAM over
>                         DRAM and viceversa.
>                         Architecture of 196 [Project based]
>                         Bus architecture.
>                         Vhdl (did you know ?)
>
>HUGES :     test - aptitude + software
>
>             questions - Assembler/linker
>                         Operating systems (Unix/MS-DOS)
>                         If you have a binary file by name test on Unix
>                         and if you type it on the command prompt what
>                         will happen ?
>                         Paging/Segmentation
>
>***** :     (I don't remember its name)
>             test - aptitude
>
>             questions - Project
>                         Operating systems
>                         C++, Software engineering
>                         ( general questions - How much you know...)
>
>
>Exter :     test - aptitude
>
>             questions - Project based
>                         Classes in C++
>                         What is OOPs
>                         What are objects in C++
>                         Polymorphism, data hiding.
>INFOSYS :   test - puzzles
>             questions - two puzzles
>A man needs 6 days to cross a desert. but one can take only 4 days
>food with him. He can take any no of assistants with him. Give a
>optimum solution.
>
>With a 11minute and 7minute hour glass how will you measure 15minute.
>
>
>TATA-ELXI : no test (all those who went on that day)
>
>             questions - Why Digital
>                         What is DSP
>                         What is sampling theorm, Its significance.
>                         Project
>CG-CoreEL : test - fully technical - digital
>             questions - A divide by 2 clock using dff
>                         Design a 4 output buzzer circuit.
>                         A visual puzzle
>                         196 architecture
>                         Max.freq of operation of digital circuits.
>
>************************************************************
